      "local_reason_code": "cloud_tenant_trust_governance_not_applicable",
      "local_deviation": "Local execution permissions remain governed by explicit sidecar and Electron capability contracts; they do not create an offline copy of tenant trust policy authority.",
      "judgment_rationale": "TrustPolicies is the canonical tenant policy administration surface. Web is degraded because an empty workspace filter is serialized as workspace_id 'default', while the backend requires a real WorkspaceModel ID in the selected tenant and provides no default-workspace resolver, so the initial list returns 404. With a valid workspace ID, list, create, and revoke remain available and tenant-member and tenant-admin enforcement remains intact, so the production actions are retained. Existing Desktop permission gates are enforcement consumers, not a policy management implementation; the Cloud route is planned and Local tenant governance is intentionally not applicable."
