      "local_deviation": "Local HITL responses and sealed replay metadata remain scoped runtime records; they must not be promoted into the Cloud tenant decision ledger without its authority.",
      "judgment_rationale": "DecisionRecords lists persisted trust decisions and approval outcomes, inspects the selected list record without a detail GET, and resolves pending approvals as allow-once, allow-always, or deny. Web is degraded because an empty workspace filter is serialized as workspace_id 'default', while the backend requires a real workspace ID in the selected tenant and has no default-workspace resolver, so the initial list returns 404. With a valid workspace ID, list, filter, inspect, and resolution remain available and tenant-member and tenant-admin enforcement remains intact, so all actions are retained. Desktop HITL UI does not provide this searchable governance ledger, and Local mode must distinguish runtime decisions from Cloud tenant records."
